Subject: fix(agents): address the configured GitHub host in the review, code and fix ops

Patch 0001 fixed this for the triage library. The same assumption is still
present in three of the other GitHub ops libraries, so every stage past triage
fails on any GitHub Enterprise install:

  ERROR: PR_URL does not match expected GitHub pattern: https://forge.internal/acme/widgets/pull/107

That is where a review run stops, before the agent does anything.
github-code-ops and github-fix-ops carry the identical pair of functions for
ISSUE_URL and PR_URL, so the code and fix stages fail the same way.

Three distinct faults, not one:

1. Validation matched https://github.com by name, rejecting a valid URL on any
   other host.
2. Parsing stripped the same literal host, so where validation did pass the
   repository was parsed wrongly.
3. forge_set_push_remote in the code and fix libraries built its remote as
   https://x-access-token:TOKEN@github.com/OWNER/REPO.git. On an enterprise
   install that does not merely fail — it sends a minted push token to
   github.com. The two libraries already read GITHUB_SERVER_URL a few lines
   further down, for the run URLs in their status comments.

There is a fourth, easy to miss: with GITHUB_SERVER_URL set to an enterprise
host, the old validation still accepted a github.com URL, because github.com
was written into the pattern rather than derived. A PR_URL from the wrong
forge passed the check. The new behaviour accepts exactly one host, whichever
one the run is executing against.

The host comes from GITHUB_SERVER_URL, defaulting to https://github.com, so
behaviour on github.com is unchanged. It is stripped as a literal prefix and
never interpolated into a regular expression, which is what patch 0001
established for the triage library, so a server URL containing regex
metacharacters cannot change what a pattern means. The shared helper also
rejects a GITHUB_SERVER_URL that is not a plain https origin, since a value
carrying a path or credentials would otherwise be spliced into URL matching.

The derivation lives in a new scripts/lib/github-host-validation.lib.sh,
mirroring scripts/lib/gitlab-host-validation.lib.sh, which has done this on the
GitLab side from the start via CI_SERVER_HOST. It does not fail closed when the
variable is unset, unlike its GitLab counterpart, because callers outside an
Actions job have no GITHUB_SERVER_URL and github.com is the right default for
them.

scripts/github-host-validation-test.sh is the GitHub counterpart of the GitLab
host-mismatch test in post-fix-test.sh. Its absence is why this survived in
four libraries after being fixed in the fifth. It covers the github.com
defaults, enterprise hosts with and without a port, the wrong-host and
lookalike-host rejections, the malformed GITHUB_SERVER_URL rejections, and both
push remotes; it fails against the unpatched libraries and passes with them.

The generated scripts that embed these libraries are regenerated here, as a
build would otherwise do: make script-build, verified with make check-bundle.

Breadboard note: this patches fullsend-ai/agents, not fullsend-ai/fullsend, and
is applied to the agents mirror by deploy/fullsend/seed/seed-upstream-agents.py.
Written to be sent upstream as-is. Add a DCO sign-off before submitting it as a
human-authored change.

Exercised locally on the review stage only; the code and fix stages have not
been run against this change.

